1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,421
Copper displaces metals below it.

2
00:00:02,421 --> 00:00:09,088
In silver nitrate it grows a glittering silver tree, and the solution turns blue.

3
00:00:09,088 --> 00:00:10,377
And here is a trap.

4
00:00:10,377 --> 00:00:16,054
Copper dissolves in iron three chloride, even though iron is above copper.

5
00:00:16,054 --> 00:00:24,895
That is because the couple involved is iron three over iron two, at plus zero point seven seven volts, which sits above copper.

6
00:00:24,895 --> 00:00:28,190
This reaction etches printed circuit boards.

